{"name":"Gilded Age","hex":"#e4b46e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Gilded Age","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The period of United States history from the end of the Civil War to the end of the 19th century, a time marked by rapid economic expansion, a lack of government regulation, and rampant corruption."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Gilded_Age"}],"entries":[{"title":"Gilded Age","blocks":[{"text":"In United States history, the Gilded Age is the period from about the late 1870s to the late 1890s, which occurred between the Reconstruction era and the Progressive Era. It was named by 1920s historians after Mark Twain's 1873 novel The Gilded Age: A Tale of Today."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/The_Breakers_Newport.jpg/330px-The_Breakers_Newport.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gilded_Age","wikidata":"Q1753636"},{"title":"Gilding","blocks":[{"text":"Gilding is a decorative technique for applying a very thin coating of gold over solid surfaces such as metal, wood, porcelain, or stone. A gilded object is also described as \"gilt\". Where metal is gilded, the metal below was traditionally silver in the West, to make silver-gilt objects, but gilt-bronze is commonly used in China, and also called ormolu if it is Western. Methods of gilding include hand application and gluing, typically of gold leaf, chemical gilding, and electroplating, the last also called gold plating. Parcel-gilt objects are only gilded over part of their surfaces. This may mean that all of the inside, and none of the outside, of a chalice or similar vessel is gilded, or that patterns or images are made up by using a combination of gilt and ungilted areas."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Gilded_frame_being_burnished_with_agate_tool.jpg/330px-Gilded_frame_being_burnished_with_agate_tool.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gilding","wikidata":"Q1334300"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/The_Gilded_Age_-_Twain_-1874_p317.png/500px-The_Gilded_Age_-_Twain_-1874_p317.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/The_Gilded_Age_-_Twain_-1874_p317.png/500px-The_Gilded_Age_-_Twain_-1874_p317.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_Gilded_Age_-_Twain_-1874_p317.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Bandits_Roost%2C_59_and_a_half_Mulberry_Street.jpg/500px-Bandits_Roost%2C_59_and_a_half_Mulberry_Street.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Bandits_Roost%2C_59_and_a_half_Mulberry_Street.jpg/1280px-Bandits_Roost%2C_59_and_a_half_Mulberry_Street.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Bandits_Roost%2C_59_and_a_half_Mulberry_Street.jpg/500px-Bandits_Roost%2C_59_and_a_half_Mulberry_Street.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABandits_Roost%2C_59_and_a_half_Mulberry_Street.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/The_Bosses_of_the_Senate_by_Joseph_Keppler_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-The_Bosses_of_the_Senate_by_Joseph_Keppler_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/The_Bosses_of_the_Senate_by_Joseph_Keppler_%28cropped%29.jpg/1280px-The_Bosses_of_the_Senate_by_Joseph_Keppler_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wi